                "entry_id": "79ebefff-91fb-3339-be21-93e03b5f0bd1",
                "word": "bonifiable",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "542ab822-e26d-4f29-a27f-61c2058439ac",
                        "entry_id": "79ebefff-91fb-3339-be21-93e03b5f0bd1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "bonifiables"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "253dfdfe-2ff5-32c8-9a39-23a727d00c2d",
                        "entry_id": "79ebefff-91fb-3339-be21-93e03b5f0bd1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pouvant être rendu meilleur, bonifié."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1be08011-76ba-4db1-ad3c-0e8088f13d3a",
                                "sense_id": "253dfdfe-2ff5-32c8-9a39-23a727d00c2d",
                                "text": "[…], la plus évidente richesse de cette terre des antipodes est sa beauté. Davantage encore que ses marées et ses rivières tropicales domestiquées, que ses pâturages « bonifiables » et que ses milliards de tonne de bauxite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b685a1cf-a01f-4d1b-a970-f05fd2a3eecb",
                                "sense_id": "253dfdfe-2ff5-32c8-9a39-23a727d00c2d",
                                "text": "Cela est un joli progrès que l’on doit en bonne partie au féminisme, au désir des pères de briser la reproduction sociale du type « homme pourvoyeur-père absent » et également, depuis quelques années, à une volonté politique qui s’est cristallisée dans la mise en place d’un congé de paternité digne de ce nom, bien que bonifiable encore."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ada8f08a-a7aa-3758-ab0f-2c3c3e436652",
                        "entry_id": "79ebefff-91fb-3339-be21-93e03b5f0bd1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui peut être avantagé par une bonification."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f53ff4b3-5041-4ab3-81da-c04904f1e49d",
                                "sense_id": "ada8f08a-a7aa-3758-ab0f-2c3c3e436652",
                                "text": "Car l’un des problèmes majeurs concerne les œuvres « qui ont recours aux codes d’écriture ou de réalisation propres au magazine ou au reportage ». Celles-ci pourraient ne plus recevoir le soutien du CNC et donc ne seraient plus, selon le vocable audiovisuel, « bonifiables »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c6584055-95fa-4426-b89d-8c6868ea48ff",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ebefff-91fb-3339-be21-93e03b5f0bd1",
                        "target_lang_word": "bonifiable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bonifiable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8d16469-72b7-3619-9538-e6096cda51e0",
                                        "entry_id": "48b40b7a-cd0a-373b-8b9a-38c6c4b1b5f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of being bonified; improvable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "328fddca-a966-45a7-a5ef-c93d3653b00c",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d16469-72b7-3619-9538-e6096cda51e0",
                                                "text": "Since glory is as bonifiable as it is intelligible, the saints in glory are glorified as much through bonifying as through understanding."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2790080-5afb-44d2-96cd-2893957d1c7e",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d16469-72b7-3619-9538-e6096cda51e0",
                                                "text": "The acts of goodness, I call bonificative, bonifiable, and bonifying, while those of greatness are magnificative, magnifiable, and magnifying, and so on for the other aforesaid dignities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbe2193c-db84-44f5-a2b5-1a95414b4fa8",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d16469-72b7-3619-9538-e6096cda51e0",
                                                "text": "I hope I'll be dreaming of someone realistically bonifiable soon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f985ec69-f81b-4201-87b1-b4c15437ce33",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d16469-72b7-3619-9538-e6096cda51e0",
                                                "text": "Moreover, anything active has to have a point of departure (in the case of the thing that produces good, he called it \"bonificative\"), an object which it affects (the \"bonifiable\"), and the act itself going from one to the other (that is, which \"bonifies\")."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a41bb8b-bc2a-47ee-b5d8-dd6d886dd8d9",
                                                "sense_id": "f8d16469-72b7-3619-9538-e6096cda51e0",
                                                "text": "She does the same thing to English. She's convinced the non-word \"bonifiable\" means certifiable or impervious to contradiction, and it's accepted as such by the people to whom she says it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
